desc: Sound Blasted! (FluidSynth port) by chmaha
tags: instrument
author: chmaha
version: 1.1
changelog:
  Fix a possible freeze (no sound, unresponsive GUI) when a looped sample wrapped many times in one block
about:
  SoundFont (SF2) General MIDI synthesizer with 16 multitimbral channels playing HL4MGM,
  FluidSynth's reverb engines (FDN, Freeverb, Dattorro) and chorus, per-channel level, pan and Follows layering,
  A4 tuning and 80 historical temperaments on the melodic channels (as in Major General MIDI),
  interpolation from none to 25-point sinc, and GM, GM2, GS and XG reset SysEx.
  Ported from FluidSynth 2.6.1 (Peter Hanappe and others, https://www.fluidsynth.org, GNU LGPL 2.1):
  sample playback, envelopes, LFOs, resonant filter, SoundFont modulators, voice allocation, MIDI handling,
  the FDN and Freeverb reverbs and the chorus match FluidSynth sample for sample.
  Sound set: HL4MGM 0.9.0 RC1 by Stardream Studios (strixSF2, Yingchun Soul), a 4 MB bank for Sound Blaster
  and AWE cards based on Yingchun Soul's 2MGM (samples from VCSL, FreePats, Iowa MIS, OSDK), Public Domain.
  JSFX code released under the GNU LGPL 2.1 or later.
  Claude generated some of this code
provides:
  Dependencies/SoundBlasted/SoundBlasted-HL4MGM.txt
  Dependencies/SoundBlasted/SoundBlasted-HL4MGM.flac

<?
